  dialogueText: 'When talking about something that existed or was true in the past,
    you can use ''ket idi'' in a historical context.

    For example, when describing
    how a place was in the past, this phrase can help connect the subject with its
    former state.

    Now, try saying ''ket idi'' yourself.'
